{
  "analysis": "The parallel OCR test seems stuck - it's been over 45 seconds for just 20 frames. Something is wrong with spawning many tesseract processes simultaneously. We should interrupt and try a different approach. Since tesseract takes 1-1.5s per frame on average, serial OCR of 950 frames would take ~20 minutes. Instead, let's work with the 1fps data we already have and improve the parser, or selectively OCR only the 5fps frames in gap regions. Alternatively, we can use ffmpeg scene detection to only extract frames when the screen changes significantly, reducing the total number of frames to OCR.",
  "plan": "Interrupt the stuck test. Then use ffmpeg scene detection to extract only keyframes where significant changes occur, which should be much fewer than 950 frames. OCR those keyframes and parse for moves.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "C-c\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /app/frames_scene /app/ocr_scene\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ffmpeg -y -i /app/video.mp4 -vf \"select='gt(scene,0.01)',showinfo\" -vsync vfr /app/frames_scene/scene_%04d.png 2>&1 | grep showinfo | wc -l\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls /app/frames_scene/*.png | wc -l\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}
